TEXT 112 24 Left 2 ;Voltagebreakdown:\nThe load held the power constant between 0.1 UN and 1.2 UN\nThe Voltage from the voltage source is relative weak since the\nimpedance is high 80Ohm inductive\nThe power is increased slowly and at approx. 550MW the voltage breakdown occur\nThe constant load needs a specific current\nThe current via the impedance leads to a voltagedrop\nWith this voltagedrop the current has to rise to hold the load constant\nand so on till the voltage reach 0.1 UN where the constant load model\nacts like a constant impedance again
TEXT 528 72 Left 2 ;Here the reltol parameter are low\nHere the vntol and abstol params are low
TEXT 472 232 Left 2 ;The parallel load model is better\nfor convergence at voltage\nbreakdown scenario\nand perhaps in other circuits
TEXT 40 112 Left 2 ;voltage is \nlow
TEXT 16 224 Left 2 !.step param UN list 360k 380k 400k 420k
TEXT 16 144 Left 2 !.param UN=360k
TEXT 16 248 Left 4 ;You can see that the voltage breakdown \nis later at networks with higher operating voltage
